\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Recommendation approved for funding in the amount of $6,000,000.00 for a new construction development of 174 multi-family affordable apartment units located at 3600 34th Street South in St. Petersburg. Total estimated development cost is $76,815,755.00. County Administrator authorized to negotiate and approve terms, conditions, and the final funding amount not to exceed the Board of County Commissioners\rquote approved amount. Staff will complete additional due diligence activities, as outlined in the Staff Report.\par
\par
Responding to comments and queries by Chair Eggers and Commissioner Flowers, Community Development Planning Division Manager Bruce Bussey, with input from Mr. Burton, provided clarifying information related to the difference in per-unit costs between Item Nos. 31 and 32, including details pertaining to variations in construction type and associated costs and additional funding sources. Mr. Bussey also explained that while the City of St. Petersburg is waiving certain development fees and providing incentives, the City is not contributing funding toward land acquisition since the County will serve as the sole landowner.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

