\par
Responding to a query by Chair Eggers, Public Works Director Kelli Hammer Levy explained that the grant will fund restoration of channels damaged during Hurricane Milton; and that, through the grant, the Natural Resources Conservation Service will fund 100% of construction and construction oversight costs.\par
\par
In response to additional queries by Chair Eggers, Ms. Levy indicated that the restoration work primarily involves repair of eroded channel banks in areas where the County has the necessary property rights or easements; that maintenance of channels located on private property is generally the responsibility of the property owners; and that County policy prohibits work on private property without the appropriate rights or authorization, including during a declared emergency.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
