\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Mr. Burke provided an overview of the annual financial audit process, including the compilation of financial statements for the Clerk\rquote s Office, the Board of County Commissioners (BCC), and Constitutional Officers. Referring to several County financial reports issued by the Clerk\rquote s Office for Fiscal Year 2025, including the Annual Debt Report, the Annual Comprehensive Financial Report, and the Citizens\rquote Guide to County Finances, he briefly discussed awards received by the County for Excellence in Financial Reporting and related that, as a result of its strong financial standing and reporting, the County will receive a reduced interest rate on bonds issued for construction of the new courthouse.\par
\par
Mr. Burke also provided brief comments related to the Clerk's Spending in the Sunshine website, which includes publicly accessible information regarding employee salaries, annual compensation, and expenditures; whereupon, he acknowledged Clerk Finance Division staff for their work to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and emphasized that the County received an unmodified financial report, which reflects the cooperation of various County departments and staff.\par
\par
Mr. Wolf related that his firm was acquired by Forvis Mazars; and that this was the first audit conducted using Forvis Mazars\rquote audit methodology; whereupon, referring to a PowerPoint presentation, he discussed required auditor communications, various reports, other deliverables, and comparative data from peer counties.\par
\par
Mr. Wolf then indicated that the County received a successful, clean audit; and that the County remains in a strong financial position; whereupon, responding to queries by Commissioner Scherer, Mr. Wolf indicated that the documents distributed to the members include budget-to-actual schedules and management discussion and analysis related to changes in the County's budget.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

