\par
Referring to language in the Staff Report for Item Nos. 17 and 18, Commissioner Scott questioned whether the contracts include provisions related to price escalators or guarantees following the initial 36-month term; whereupon, following brief comments by Mr. Burton regarding the scope of Item No. 17, Commissioner Scott clarified that he meant to refer to Item Nos. 18 and 19.\par
\par
Responding to queries by Commissioner Scott regarding Item Nos. 18 and 19, Construction and Property Management Director Bill Greer indicated that the contracts do not include price escalators; and that, should the two 12-month term extensions be exercised, pricing established for the initial 36-month term would remain in effect.\par
\par
In response to a query by Chair Eggers, Mr. Greer confirmed that the County may terminate or adjust the contracts and scale back activity should funding become unavailable; whereupon, he also provided details regarding the benefits of consolidating multiple contracts under Item No. 18, including efficiency of service and increased competition among vendors.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

