\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Referring to a PowerPoint presentation titled \i FY27 Maximum Millage Rates Consensus, \i0 Office of Management and Budget Director Chris Rose indicated that, at the request of the Property Appraiser, the County must establish maximum millage rates by July 28; that Truth in Millage notices will be mailed on August 17; and that, following certification, the millage rates may only be decreased; whereupon, he reviewed the maximum millage rates which are being proposed by staff, the required voting thresholds for approval, and the budget timeline.\par
\par
Mr. Burton then indicated that staff is seeking consensus from the members regarding the proposed maximum millage rates in order to transmit them to the Property Appraiser. He also noted that the proposed budget will be presented on August 11; and that staff is continuing to finalize budget issues with several departments.\par
\par
Responding to comments and queries by Chair Eggers and Commissioner Flowers, Mr. Burton discussed the upcoming budget process and provided information regarding potential impacts of a proposed State constitutional amendment related to property taxes on future County budgets, including potential reductions to programs, staffing, and service levels should the amendment be approved; whereupon, Chair Eggers confirmed that there is a consensus to establish the maximum millage rates as presented by staff.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

