\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Chair Eggers indicated that the first public hearing for the tentative budget has resumed; whereupon, Mr. Burton noted that Mr. Rose will now review corrections to the initial proposed budget and the effects of the Board\rquote s new proposed action.\par
\par
Mr. Rose indicated that he misspoke in stating that the tentative budget as proposed is a 0.16% decrease over the aggregate rolled-back rate of 6.1284; and that the correct number is a 0.48% increase over the aggregate rolled-back rate of 6.1284, which he must read into the record for the State. He reported that the budget was proposed at 4.5423 mills on the Countywide General Fund; that, with the amendments made, the new millage rate would be 4.4989 mills in the Countywide General Fund; that this amounts to a 0.71% change, which is 57.9% of rollback; and that the new aggregate millage rate is 6.1141, which is 0.23% below the rolled-back rate.\par
\par
Commissioner Peters then made a motion to adopt the budget as amended, which was seconded by Commissioner Flowers; whereupon, Attorney White requested that the members first make a motion regarding the millage rate. Following clarifying comments by Mr. Burton and Chief Assistant County Attorney Don Crowell, Commissioner Peters made a motion to accept the changes to the proposed budget.\par
\par
Attorney White recommended that the changes to the budget be enunciated along with the motion to change the budget prior to taking a vote regarding the tentative millage. Responding to comments by Commissioner Peters, Mr. Burton then clarified that the changes to the budget include funding $667,000.00 using one-time money from reserves for social action funding; that the millage rate will be affected as a result; and that Commissioner Peters is also recommending the other proposed changes outlined in the aforementioned memorandum reviewed by Mr. Rose earlier in the meeting; whereupon, Commissioner Peters confirmed that is her motion.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

