\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Initiation of litigation ratified.\par
\par
Attorney White indicated that the case referenced in the agenda item relates to an illicit discharge into the Cross Bayou Canal and other environmental degradation; and that staff determined that an emergency order was required.\par
\par
Upon the request of Chair Eggers, Public Works Director Kelli Hammer Levy indicated that there is a sinkhole located on County Road 95; and that, when the sinkhole fills, it overflows and floods onto the road. Ms. Levy noted that, when the area was developed, property owners requested installation of private pump stations; and that one of the aforementioned property owners failed to maintain their pump station; whereupon, she briefly summarized a court order requiring the property owner to maintain and operate the pump station in accordance with its approved site plan, as well as the County's subsequent coordination with the property owner to lower water levels and prevent roadway flooding.\cf1\f1\fs22\par
}

