Responding to queries by Commissioner Scherer, Chief Human Resources Officer Wade Childress indicated that this Medicare Advantage contract is financed by the federal government; that the County pays a portion of the contract and anticipates a 10% increase in payment over the previous contract with Aetna as the County transitions to UnitedHealthcare; that the two-year rate guarantee consists of an increase of 5% per year; and that the County and its retirees pay approximately 31% and 68%, respectively, of the cost of the contract.\par
